WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:02.868
-I'm so happy you're here! -I'm on "Jimmy Fallon"?!

00:00:02.868 --> 00:00:04.501
Oh, my gosh. -Oh, my gosh. Come on.

00:00:04.501 --> 00:00:06.067
-Wow. I can't believe this right now.

00:00:06.067 --> 00:00:07.767
You guys have no idea. -No, please.

00:00:07.767 --> 00:00:10.834
-No, no. It's just so exciting.

00:00:10.834 --> 00:00:12.234
I'm in the chair.

00:00:12.234 --> 00:00:14.167
-You are in the chair. We're doing this.

00:00:14.167 --> 00:00:16.200
I met you last year

00:00:16.200 --> 00:00:18.334
at Justin Timberlake's golf tournament.

00:00:18.334 --> 00:00:20.434
-That's right. -It was 8:00 a.m., right?

00:00:20.434 --> 00:00:21.834
-Yeah, the 8AM Tournament in Vegas.

00:00:21.834 --> 00:00:23.334
-How fun was that? -It was so much fun.

00:00:23.334 --> 00:00:24.801
-That was one of the most fun things.

00:00:24.801 --> 00:00:28.801
And you were so funny and you were so nice and cool, and we --

00:00:28.801 --> 00:00:30.601
I think -- Did you end up winning?

00:00:30.601 --> 00:00:32.868
-Yeah, that's right. You know, what's funny about that

00:00:32.868 --> 00:00:36.467
is one of the prizes at the golf tournament was two tickets

00:00:36.467 --> 00:00:38.100
to "The Tonight Show with Jimmy Fallon."

00:00:38.100 --> 00:00:40.267
-Yeah. -And I won those tickets.

00:00:40.267 --> 00:00:41.801
-You won them. Yeah.

00:00:41.801 --> 00:00:44.701
[ Cheers and applause ] -So I -- Thank you.

00:00:44.701 --> 00:00:46.067
You think I'm here for "Ant-Man."

00:00:46.067 --> 00:00:47.701
I'm really here because I won two tickets

00:00:47.701 --> 00:00:50.167
at a golf tournament. And I brought my mom.

00:00:50.167 --> 00:00:51.601
She's in the audience tonight.

00:00:51.601 --> 00:00:53.267
-Your mom actually is -- [ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:53.267 --> 00:00:55.901
-Yeah. -Where's Mom?

00:00:55.901 --> 00:00:57.667
Hi, Mom!

00:00:57.667 --> 00:00:59.601
[ Cheers and applause ] -That's right.

00:00:59.601 --> 00:01:01.868
-But that's not what -- -And that's why I'm here.

00:01:01.868 --> 00:01:04.267
-That's not why you're here. -I thought that it'd be okay

00:01:04.267 --> 00:01:05.667
if I sat up here, you know, for a minute.

00:01:05.667 --> 00:01:06.968
-Of the two tickets that you're using.

00:01:06.968 --> 00:01:08.434
-Just to talk for a second. -So you're only

00:01:08.434 --> 00:01:10.000
using one ticket then use another one tomorrow?

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:11.100
-I can come back, right?

00:01:11.100 --> 00:01:12.434
-You can come back whenever you want.

00:01:12.434 --> 00:01:13.501
-Thank you.

00:01:13.501 --> 00:01:14.834
-You're a great golfer, by the way.

00:01:14.834 --> 00:01:16.434
-Thank you. You are, too. And you know what?

00:01:16.434 --> 00:01:17.868
It's a dream to be here tonight.

00:01:17.868 --> 00:01:21.534
So, I just remembered that you had that great bunker shot.

00:01:21.534 --> 00:01:23.367
You know, the one that you made? You made one shot.

00:01:23.367 --> 00:01:25.033
-The one they showed on the show every day

00:01:25.033 --> 00:01:26.901
for like three months? -I know the feeling.

00:01:26.901 --> 00:01:31.434
So, to honor that amazing shot, I got something for you.

00:01:31.434 --> 00:01:33.634
I got you a custom wedge.

00:01:33.634 --> 00:01:36.434
And it says "Jimmy's Lucky Wedge" on it.

00:01:36.434 --> 00:01:38.400
Look! -This is insane.

00:01:38.400 --> 00:01:40.000
You don't have to get me anything.

00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:42.601
-And I put little ants -- Well, I wanted --

00:01:42.601 --> 00:01:44.467
-That is so nice. -Now it's really lucky.

00:01:44.467 --> 00:01:46.133
You're always going to be lucky now.

00:01:46.133 --> 00:01:48.267
-Now it's part of my bag. It's in my bag forever.

00:01:48.267 --> 00:01:51.067
-I got you a driver with Cassie Lang's power suit,

00:01:51.067 --> 00:01:53.033
her super-suit colors. -No.

00:01:53.033 --> 00:01:55.334
-So you can hit it like a superhero just like me.

00:01:55.334 --> 00:01:56.501
-Exactly right.

00:01:56.501 --> 00:01:57.801
-Yeah, and then next year, you know,

00:01:57.801 --> 00:02:00.567
maybe I'll have to try a little harder to beat you.

00:02:00.567 --> 00:02:03.167
-Yeah. Who did win? Oh, no. You know who won?

00:02:03.167 --> 00:02:04.767
-Mahomes. -Mahomes and Kelce.

00:02:04.767 --> 00:02:06.067
-Mahomes, I'm coming for you.

00:02:06.067 --> 00:02:07.701
-Yeah, we're coming for you, Mahomes -- this year.

00:02:07.701 --> 00:02:09.634
a-Yeah, that's right. -When did you start golfing?

00:02:09.634 --> 00:02:11.234
Here. This looks like you're very young.

00:02:11.234 --> 00:02:12.434
-That's me and my dad.

00:02:12.434 --> 00:02:13.968
-Aww. -In my little Ralph Lauren.

00:02:13.968 --> 00:02:15.834
You know, I've been golfing my whole life.

00:02:15.834 --> 00:02:18.434
It's just -- It's my backup plan. You know?

00:02:18.434 --> 00:02:19.934
-Yeah, exactly. Right? -Yeah.

00:02:19.934 --> 00:02:22.901
-I mean, you played at some of the most iconic courses,

00:02:22.901 --> 00:02:27.467
but you went viral for this shot that you made at Pebble Beach.

00:02:27.467 --> 00:02:28.667
-I did. -Watch this.

00:02:28.667 --> 00:02:30.734
And, yeah, listen.

00:02:30.734 --> 00:02:32.367
-Oh, God. -Oh, nice swing.

00:02:32.367 --> 00:02:34.000
-Yeah. -What a swing there.

00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:36.834
-God, what a good swing. -Where's that going, Steve?

00:02:36.834 --> 00:02:38.701
-It's a million-dollar hole, you know.

00:02:38.701 --> 00:02:41.067
-Yes!

00:02:41.067 --> 00:02:42.734
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:42.734 --> 00:02:44.067
-Are you kidding me?!

00:02:44.067 --> 00:02:46.234
[ Cheers and applause ] -Well, thank you. Thank you.

00:02:46.234 --> 00:02:48.400
-And was that Bill Murray? -That was Bill.

00:02:48.400 --> 00:02:50.334
You know, that's where the two things

00:02:50.334 --> 00:02:51.501
that I do really come together.

00:02:51.501 --> 00:02:53.334
'Cause I was acting like a pro golfer.

00:02:53.334 --> 00:02:55.167
I'm really not a -- I'm okay.

00:02:55.167 --> 00:02:57.300
That was the only good shot I hit all day.

00:02:57.300 --> 00:02:59.734
It's the only one that's on TV. -That's all you need.

00:02:59.734 --> 00:03:02.067
-Yeah, they would show my swing and then cut away

00:03:02.067 --> 00:03:04.467
so that no one saw where the ball went.

00:03:04.467 --> 00:03:06.234
But I really had to pull it together, you know?

00:03:06.234 --> 00:03:08.234
Bill and Macklemore were cheering me on.

00:03:08.234 --> 00:03:09.734
They were like, "Kathryn, let's go."

00:03:09.734 --> 00:03:10.934
And I was like, "Okay."

00:03:10.934 --> 00:03:12.200
So it's the only good shot I hit that day.

00:03:12.200 --> 00:03:15.033
-So, you hear Bill Murray go, "What a swing."

00:03:15.033 --> 00:03:16.100
-I know.

00:03:16.100 --> 00:03:17.601
-Is there pressure golfing with Bill?

00:03:17.601 --> 00:03:21.033
-You know, the pressure was not Bill, but the pressure was TV.

00:03:21.033 --> 00:03:24.200
I was, like, "I got to show everyone I'm a real golfer."

00:03:24.200 --> 00:03:26.234
And Bill was like, "Kathryn, you're just an actor.

00:03:26.234 --> 00:03:27.634
It's okay." [ Laughter ]

00:03:27.634 --> 00:03:29.767
And then I hit that great shot after he said that.

00:03:29.767 --> 00:03:32.067
-And then you're like, "Am I? Or am I great a golfer?"

00:03:32.067 --> 00:03:34.334
-"Am I a good golfer or am I an actor? I don't know."

00:03:34.334 --> 00:03:36.334
But then a couple months later, my mom's like,

00:03:36.334 --> 00:03:38.367
"Kathryn, I have Bill Murray for you."

00:03:38.367 --> 00:03:41.000
I'm like, "What? Bill Murray?"

00:03:41.000 --> 00:03:42.434
She's like, "Yeah. Here."

00:03:42.434 --> 00:03:44.868
And he's like, "Kathryn, I've been thinking.

00:03:44.868 --> 00:03:47.868
I think I want to join the Marvel Universe.

00:03:47.868 --> 00:03:50.067
And I was just gonna ask you if it was okay

00:03:50.067 --> 00:03:51.868
if I join "Ant-Man."

00:03:51.868 --> 00:03:54.133
And I was like, "Uh, yeah, Bill, that's cool.

00:03:54.133 --> 00:03:55.701
That's cool with me.

00:03:55.701 --> 00:03:57.267
Maybe there's someone else to talk to."

00:03:57.267 --> 00:03:58.868
But I think he had, like, an offer,

00:03:58.868 --> 00:04:00.567
and he was just calling to be like,

00:04:00.567 --> 00:04:02.133
"Are we gonna play golf together?"

00:04:02.133 --> 00:04:03.868
Michael Douglas golfs, as well.

00:04:03.868 --> 00:04:05.667
We didn't get to golf, though,

00:04:05.667 --> 00:04:07.400
because London, you know, it was rainy.

00:04:07.400 --> 00:04:10.100
And it turns out Marvel movies are very intense

00:04:10.100 --> 00:04:12.334
and I didn't want to golf.

00:04:12.334 --> 00:04:13.734
[ Laughter ] -Yeah. You didn't want to.

00:04:13.734 --> 00:04:15.834
Yeah, but, I mean, you're in a Marvel movie.

00:04:15.834 --> 00:04:17.601
You're in one of the biggest things,

00:04:17.601 --> 00:04:19.267
machines in the whole wide world.

00:04:19.267 --> 00:04:20.801
They make the best, most fun movies.

00:04:20.801 --> 00:04:22.367
What happens when you get that call?

00:04:22.367 --> 00:04:24.868
And you're like -- you're going to be in "Ant-Man and the Wasp."

00:04:24.868 --> 00:04:28.133
-Well, you know, they told me that I got the offer,

00:04:28.133 --> 00:04:29.667
and I didn't believe it.

00:04:29.667 --> 00:04:31.133
And then I got the announcement.

00:04:31.133 --> 00:04:32.901
I saw it, you know. Still didn't believe it.

00:04:32.901 --> 00:04:35.133
Then I had to hold it as a secret for a year

00:04:35.133 --> 00:04:37.200
while we filmed the movie, and I still didn't believe it.

00:04:37.200 --> 00:04:38.501
And then I watched it last night,

00:04:38.501 --> 00:04:40.367
and I still don't believe I'm in the movie!

00:04:40.367 --> 00:04:41.901
-You are definitely in the movie.

00:04:41.901 --> 00:04:43.734
-I saw my name. It was on there.

00:04:43.734 --> 00:04:46.434
The Marvel Comics. I'm like, "What?!"

00:04:46.434 --> 00:04:48.667
-Yeah. -And then it said my name.

00:04:48.667 --> 00:04:50.234
And I'm like, "Are you sure?" -Yeah.

00:04:50.234 --> 00:04:52.100
-Doesn't even look like me, really.

00:04:52.100 --> 00:04:53.701
But it's me. -It is you.

00:04:53.701 --> 00:04:55.267
Paul Rudd, who is -- -Is the best.

00:04:55.267 --> 00:04:57.167
-Friend of the show. One of the funniest --

00:04:57.167 --> 00:04:58.934
-Funniest person in the world. Behind you, Jimmy.

00:04:58.934 --> 00:05:00.667
-Thank you. Of course. Thank you.

00:05:00.667 --> 00:05:02.934
And you. Then Paul Rudd. So, third.

00:05:02.934 --> 00:05:05.901
-Yeah, third. -But he plays your dad.

00:05:05.901 --> 00:05:07.934
-Yeah. -How is he to work with?

00:05:07.934 --> 00:05:09.367
-How lucky am I? -Yeah, I mean, please.

00:05:09.367 --> 00:05:11.934
-I mean, yes, it was a dream come true

00:05:11.934 --> 00:05:13.300
to be a part of the Marvel Universe.

00:05:13.300 --> 00:05:17.033
But then I got Paul Rudd. I laughed every day on set.

00:05:17.033 --> 00:05:19.133
You know how great he is. -He's ridiculously funny.

00:05:19.133 --> 00:05:22.133
-He made me funny, you know? He brought it out of me.

00:05:22.133 --> 00:05:24.767
And I couldn't have asked for a better experience.

00:05:24.767 --> 00:05:26.000
No, never.

00:05:26.000 --> 00:05:27.133
-Did you ruin takes by laughing?

00:05:27.133 --> 00:05:28.534
-Oh, for sure.

00:05:28.534 --> 00:05:31.734
Actually, I'm a little mad at him because I can tell --

00:05:31.734 --> 00:05:33.567
I laugh in every single scene in the movie.

00:05:33.567 --> 00:05:35.067
Like, I break in every scene.

00:05:35.067 --> 00:05:37.200
And there was one day we had 500 extras.

00:05:37.200 --> 00:05:38.934
Okay? 500!

00:05:38.934 --> 00:05:41.734
We had 10 explosions, bombs, fire.

00:05:41.734 --> 00:05:44.234
Serious stuff where you can really, really get hurt.

00:05:44.234 --> 00:05:46.734
And I was nervous. He could tell.

00:05:46.734 --> 00:05:48.534
And he looked at me, and he's like, "Are you nervous?"

00:05:48.534 --> 00:05:50.000
I'm like, "Yeah." He's like, "You got this.

00:05:50.000 --> 00:05:53.234
You can do it. Whatever you do, don't laugh."

00:05:53.234 --> 00:05:55.400
"Action!" Couldn't stop laughing.

00:05:55.400 --> 00:05:57.901
I couldn't stop. I couldn't keep it together.

00:05:57.901 --> 00:05:59.801
-That's the perfect way to do it. "Just don't laugh. Action."

00:05:59.801 --> 00:06:01.167
-He was the worst.

00:06:01.167 --> 00:06:04.400
The worst part is like -- it's not even a funny joke.

00:06:04.400 --> 00:06:06.434
-But it gets you the giggles, then you can't stop.

00:06:06.434 --> 00:06:07.934
-Yeah, I got the giggles.

00:06:07.934 --> 00:06:10.400
So then there's bodies flying, dirt flying.

00:06:10.400 --> 00:06:12.767
The director, Peyton Reed, is like, "Kathryn?

00:06:12.767 --> 00:06:15.000
Are you smiling? Are you laughing?"

00:06:15.000 --> 00:06:16.400
I'm just smiling ear to ear

00:06:16.400 --> 00:06:18.601
as people are dying and explosions are happening.

00:06:18.601 --> 00:06:20.334
-You can't use any of this material.

00:06:20.334 --> 00:06:21.934
"We can't use any of this, Kathryn."

00:06:21.934 --> 00:06:23.267
-No. Hour reset.

00:06:23.267 --> 00:06:25.400
Paul's just laughing at me like, "Ha-ha. Got you."

00:06:25.400 --> 00:06:27.300
I got him back, though. I did make him break.

00:06:27.300 --> 00:06:29.534
And you know he's really good at not breaking.

00:06:29.534 --> 00:06:31.701
So I got him back. -You got him to break?

00:06:31.701 --> 00:06:33.534
-Yeah. You know, it's not bad.

00:06:33.534 --> 00:06:35.067
-Got Ant-Man to laugh. -Yeah.

00:06:35.067 --> 00:06:36.400
-How do we set up the movie?

00:06:36.400 --> 00:06:37.834
-Okay. -"Quantumania."

00:06:37.834 --> 00:06:39.834
-So, if you're a fan of "Ant-Man,"

00:06:39.834 --> 00:06:41.367
you know you're going to laugh a little bit.

00:06:41.367 --> 00:06:44.067
And you've got Cassie Lang and her dad reconnecting.

00:06:44.067 --> 00:06:45.667
It's the heart of the story.

00:06:45.667 --> 00:06:49.033
But the movie -- I just saw it. It's huge.

00:06:49.033 --> 00:06:50.601
It's way bigger than I thought.

00:06:50.601 --> 00:06:53.767
-Really? -Like, Kang -- It's amazing.

00:06:53.767 --> 00:06:56.100
I love the movie, and I think everyone's going to love it.

00:06:56.100 --> 00:06:59.167
-Okay. Good. Alright. Good. I want to show a clip.

00:06:59.167 --> 00:07:01.501
This is a big deal!

00:07:01.501 --> 00:07:03.200
Here's Kathryn Newton

00:07:03.200 --> 00:07:05.667
In "Ant-Man and the Wasp: Quantumania."

00:07:05.667 --> 00:07:07.167
Take a look at this.

00:07:07.167 --> 00:07:09.200
-You know, I promised your mom that you would only use

00:07:09.200 --> 00:07:11.033
this stuff when one of us was around.

00:07:11.033 --> 00:07:13.267
It's really dangerous tech. -I know it's dangerous.

00:07:13.267 --> 00:07:14.901
-What if the cops took it from you?

00:07:14.901 --> 00:07:17.501
Hmm? What if you lost it? -I didn't lose the suit!

00:07:17.501 --> 00:07:19.467
-You have a suit? Wait. You have a suit?!

00:07:19.467 --> 00:07:21.167
-I know how to take care of myself, okay?

00:07:21.167 --> 00:07:24.300
Trust me. I'm pretty good at it by now.

00:07:24.300 --> 00:07:26.234
-Ouch.

00:07:27.834 --> 00:07:29.434
-Look, I didn't mean it like that. I'm sorry.

00:07:29.434 --> 00:07:32.267
-I know. It's ok-- It's alright. I get it.

00:07:32.267 --> 00:07:34.934
I just think you should get to have a normal life.

00:07:34.934 --> 00:07:37.834
-Dad, a guy dressed like a bee tried to kill me in my room

00:07:37.834 --> 00:07:39.767
when I was 6.

00:07:39.767 --> 00:07:42.968
I've never had a normal life.

00:07:42.968 --> 00:07:44.801
-How about some music?

00:07:44.801 --> 00:07:47.234
-"And in that moment, all I could think was,

00:07:47.234 --> 00:07:49.501
how did the Hulk turn me into a baby?

00:07:49.501 --> 00:07:52.834
Will I be a baby forever? Am I the Hulk's baby?"

00:07:52.834 --> 00:07:54.767
-Dad, are you listening to your own book?

00:07:54.767 --> 00:07:56.501
-"But I was ready for anything." -Hmm?

00:07:56.501 --> 00:07:59.133
[ Cheers and applause ] -Come on!

00:07:59.133 --> 00:08:00.501
Thank you again for this.

00:08:00.501 --> 00:08:02.400
-Thank you. -That is so thoughtful.

00:08:02.400 --> 00:08:04.434
And, really, I'm so happy you're here.

00:08:04.434 --> 00:08:06.701
Come back whenever. -I love it. I'd love to.

00:08:06.701 --> 00:08:08.434
-You can bring Mom, too. -Okay.

00:08:08.434 --> 00:08:09.667
-Kathryn Newton, everyone.

00:08:09.667 --> 00:08:11.767
"Ant-Man and the Wasp: Quantumania"

00:08:11.767 --> 00:08:14.801
is in theaters and IMAX February 17th.

